     1                                  ; E5 C2 (day2 round 2 agent E5): C1 + V6-case turn sync. The no-V6 je jumps 2 bytes into the dec (decodes as
     2                                  ; mov dh,0), and the startup band math uses a memory divisor, so phoenix_init starts at instr 25 in both cases
     3                                  ; (DET2 and C1: 26 when a V6-family team is present; the V6-family B itself starts its phoenix at 25). B 234 B.
     4                                  ; E5 C1 (day2 round 2 agent E5, base DET2 = rev2): B-only, zero-byte, turn-neutral reorder of the startup so every
     5                                  ; hook-cell write lands on one fixed round whether or not a V6-family team is present (DET2's writes moved by one
     6                                  ; round in the V6 case): cmp [4A17h] 4, [0CC13h] 5, [9769h] 6, [5D13h] 7, [4A17h] 8, INT87 14 (DET2 15/16); the
     7                                  ; je/dec moved after the INT87 (flags survive mov/std/int 87h/cld). Rebuilds the useful part of the round-1 S4/LATE
     8                                  ; reorders on DET2: [5D13h] now after the V6 family's write (B 5) and the m050/Synthesis/FixedToggle A write (4);
     9                                  ; [9769h] back before Registered_Winners2's INT87 (9). phoenix_init rounds unchanged (25 / 26).
    10                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided code (see the provenance comments below); E5 edits by agent2 day2 role E5.
    11                                  ; D4 DET2: DET with B's [5D13h]/[0CC13h] writes back at instr 4/5 (rev1 rounds). DET's instr-3 [0CC13h]
    12                                  ; write tied with the zchain/zrl03/ah02 A write (instr 3) and lost the p0f13 hook half the time (screen n6sgd).
    13                                  ; D4 DET (day2, base rev1 KPHL): adaptive whole-team lattice. If a V6-family team is present (its B writes
    14                                  ; [4A17h] at instr 3; no other team in our fields writes that cell), every stream of ours (A, B, captured zombies)
    15                                  ; uses FAR_SEG 0FFAh = lattice 42h (10h below the V6-family 52h lattice, measured +0.28/+0.24 on leader2/3 cohorts
    16                                  ; in D4 W42 screen 0b3hc); otherwise FAR_SEG 0FFBh = 52h as in rev1 (W42's plain 2025/strong cost avoided).
    17                                  ; Detection: our B now writes [4A17h] late (instr 7), so at A's instr 5 and B's instr 5 the cell is still CCCCh
    18                                  ; unless a V6-family B wrote it at instr 3. A keeps the bit in BP; B patches the low byte of its own phoenix
    19                                  ; 'or dx,0FFBh' immediate (dec -> 0FAh) before any captured zombie can reach phoenix_init.
    20                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided code (see the provenance comments below); DET edits by agent2 day2 role D4.
    21                                  ; COMBINE (night combination coordinator, 2026-10-04, base rev0): KPHL = KP + h34 (B099 KPH_B) + locpatA (B092 KL_A). A = KL_A unchanged; B = B099 KPH_B.
    22                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided code; V6nohunt and all night edits by agent2 roles (see FINDINGS.md).
    23                                  ; B099 (wave 10, domain 9 R5-cost): KPH = B094 KP + B089 h34 (CX=0 zombie path mov bp,3400h -> 7000h, 1 byte).
    24                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided; V6nohunt by agent2; K by A031 (E1+SD+Z1 by A031/A022/A026); p0f13 by B064/B084; KP by B094; h34 by B089.
    25                                  ; B094 (wave 9, domain 4 R5-cost): KP = A031 K (E1+SD+Z1) + B084 p0f13 B edits ported onto K_B (Z1+SD).
    26                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided; V6nohunt by agent2; Z1 by A026, SD by A022, E1/K by A031; p0f by B064, p0f13 by B084.
    27                                  ; p0f13 edits: startup push cs/pop es -> mov [0CC13h],bx + les di,[si+es_ptr] (INT87 stays instr 12); both b/d searches
    28                                  ;   (startup and zom20a path) use window 0F EB F9 CC -> 0F FF 26 13 (patched tail = jmp [0CC13h]).
    29                                  ; Port note: in the zom20a path DX is now 0CCF9h after INT87, so Z1's int 86h there would write FF 1F F9 CC junk
    30                                  ;   over E1's A block (0FF80h..007Fh). It is replaced by mov dx,0CCCCh (same instruction count, no INT86 there);
    31                                  ;   E1's A block already covers 0FF80h..007Fh. The b/d (CX=0) path INT86 block is unchanged.
    32                                  bits 16
    33                                  
    34                                  ; Good_Test V6 warrior 2 (friend-provided; reconstructed source in
    35                                  ; study-notes/good-test-v6/source/). agent2 label form: hard-coded internal
    36                                  ; offsets replaced by label arithmetic with the original operand widths.
    37                                  ; agent2 night A026 variant Z1 (base rev0 = V6nohunt B): captured zombies spend
    38                                  ; their own INT 86h charge (2 per zombie, unused before) on FF 1F CC CC decoy
    39                                  ; blocks for the FF1FCCCC INT87 searchers.
    40                                  ;  - zom20a path (CX!=0): after its b/d INT87, mov ax,1FFFh; int 86h with
    41                                  ;    DI=0, DF=1, DX=CCCCh -> block 0FF04h..0003h (no code is ever loaded below
    42                                  ;    400h or above FC00h; page FFh and 00h:00-03 hold no anchor of our 400h
    43                                  ;    lattice at 52h).
    44                                  ;  - b/d path (CX=0): the worthless 0E070E17 CC counter-bomb INT87 is replaced
    45                                  ;    by a block next to the zombie's own body (BX = own load address + 3):
    46                                  ;    [X+68h, X+168h), X = (BX and FC00h). Inside the zombie's MIN_GAP zone
    47                                  ;    and on pages 4k / 4k+1 outside in-page 52h-67h of pages 4k, so it can
    48                                  ;    hit neither loaded code nor any anchor/worker of our lattice.
    49                                  ;  - zombie band math uses 16-bit DIV (same AX, 2 instructions fewer), so both
    50                                  ;    zombie paths reach phoenix_init on the same turn as in rev0.
    51                                  ; B's own startup is unchanged.
    52                                  
    53                                  ; A031 K = A026 Z1 (zombie INT86 blocks) + A022 SD (phoenix_init mov cx,10; dead mov dx,[4A17h] dropped; db 0CCh,0CCh after the worker). B startup unchanged.
